-- table, column, constraint, index or row changes.
--
--   live_sessions             one live session of one community: the aggregate
--                             root, whose row is the lock for everything below;
--                             at most one live per community
--                             (live_sessions_one_live_per_community)
--   live_speaker_requests     the raise-hand queue: at most one open request per
--                             person and session; a raise after a closed one is
--                             a new row
--   live_presenter_grants     the screen-share slot: at most one open grant per
--                             session; a later claim is a new row
--   live_moderation_actions   every moderation act, written in the transaction
--                             that makes the change; a reason is a code, never
--                             free text
--
-- Community and account ids are plain text: no foreign key leaves Live's
-- tables, and none enters them. Inside Live every key is session_id →
-- live_sessions, RESTRICT: nothing is deleted (Q3). Every enumerated column's
-- CHECK lists exactly the domain's constant.
